WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.770
At evening prayer in a monastery, the monks
sing with no instruments and no harmony.

2
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.570
Just one melody, sung together,
its rhythm following the words.

3
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.100
It is written in square notes,
on a stave of only four lines.

4
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.280
This chant is named after
a pope who died in 604.

5
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.100
So why do Christians sing
their prayers at all?

6
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.810
And why keep chants over 1,000 years old?

7
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.420
In this mission, you'll meet psalms,
plainchant and traditional hymns.

8
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.240
Then you'll weigh up whether traditional
music is the best music for worship.

9
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.900
Your mission: find out why
Christians sing their prayers,

10
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.330
and why ancient chants are still sung.
